          "The nickname is older and more formal than it sounds, and it was never just household speech. The early printed editions used it on their own title pages, which open Narek girk, the Narek book, and the Mekhitarist scholar Gabriel Awetikian titled his Venice commentary Narek, Book of Prayers. By the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries, then, learned publishers were using the nickname as a bibliographic title, while critical scholarship kept the formal title Matean voghbergutean.",
