          "The book left the monastery early and entered ordinary homes, and its life there is as much a part of its history as its manuscripts. Families who could not read grabar owned it, kept it with their valuables, and treated it as an object of standing, not a text to study. By the medieval period it was already called the Narek and described as a medicine of life.",
