          "Mtnadzor is a collection of eighteen short stories by Aksel Bakunts, published at Yerevan in 1927. It was the first book of fiction he published, and it turned an agronomist who wrote into a writer. Suren Aghababyan, author of the standard study of Bakunts, opens his account of it by calling it one of those books whose appearance fixes a new date in the history of a literature.",
