          "Manasyan suggests reading the book through what she calls literary geography, and sets Bakunts beside the diaspora writer Hamasteghd. Hamasteghd built a village-world; Bakunts built a point-world. In her reading, Mtnadzor is less a setting than the rim of Bakunts's world: a single dense point where everything begins, continues and returns.",
