          "The stories are short and tightly constructed. Manasyan calls the technique photographic: dense episodes, short white-hot tonalities, terse sentences. Her examples are the fight between the hunter and the bear, and the moment when the whole conflict between Avi and Panin rests on one contrast of colour: one man's face is like canvas, the other's like a red beetroot.",
          "Memory is part of the structure, not a lyrical extra. Manasyan makes this point against Ishkhanyan, who had read Bakunts's recollection scenes as a way of making the past present. For her, Dilan's recollection in Միրհավ is not lyrical narration but the symphony of a life with its contrary deviations, and the teacher's in Խոնարհ աղջիկը continues a drama instead of telling of a love that never happened. Aghababyan draws the same distinction in technical terms: Միրհավ is built on musical retrospection, Խոնարհ աղջիկը on painterly retrospection.",
          "Aghababyan also credits Bakunts with a formal innovation. Armenian prose before him, he says, had no way to run two planes of narration inside a single syntactic unit, and Bakunts made this a recognised part of the form. Խոնարհ աղջիկը, which has both a narrator and an author, is where he shows it. Aghababyan also names what carries the weight: the Bakuntsian sub-text is the continuation of the text. In Գյուլբահարի համար the story runs along with no deep current until a village court convicts not the accused but the villagers who had persecuted the priest. It ends on a man left standing as a question mark.",
