          "There is one well-documented screen version. Բաղդասարը բաժանվում է կնոջից (Baghdasar Divorces His Wife) was produced by Armenfilm in 1976 and released the following April. Grigor Melik-Avagyan directed it from a screenplay by Aghasi Ayvazyan, with Mher Mkrtchyan, the best-known Armenian comic actor of the period, as Baghdasar.",
          "Two qualifications come with it, both from the state film archive's own catalogue record. It is a feature film, not a filmed stage production, and it is based on motifs from the play, not adapted from its text. It also renames its hero: the film's Բաղդասար is the Eastern Armenian form, where the play's Պաղտասար is the Western one. The difference is worth knowing, because in English search results the film reliably ranks above the play, and the two are easy to mistake for one work.",
